WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.006
The Department Portal collects clean, validated data from university departments for submission to NAAC.

2
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:12.877
It follows the same five-step collection approach as the institute portal, with department names as the starting point.

3
00:00:12.877 --> 00:00:22.174
The steps are department selection, email and passcode verification, criterion and metric selection, supporting document upload, and final review and submission.

4
00:00:22.874 --> 00:00:26.037
In step one, the user selects their department.

5
00:00:26.037 --> 00:00:31.892
Examples include Academics, Examination, Finance, Human Resources, IT, and the Library.

6
00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:36.670
In step two, the user enters the authorised email address and passcode.

7
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:40.978
The displayed email and passcode are demonstration placeholders.

8
00:00:40.978 --> 00:00:45.285
This connects the reporting workflow to the selected department.

9
00:00:45.985 --> 00:00:51.115
In step three, the user selects the criterion and metric for the department’s submission.

10
00:00:51.115 --> 00:00:56.245
They download the predefined template, complete its required columns, and upload the CSV.

11
00:00:56.245 --> 00:01:03.335
As in the institute workflow, Google Apps Script defines the column structure and validation rules for the selected metric.

12
00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:07.260
The portal includes separate Nil and Not Applicable options.

13
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.528
Nil means the metric is relevant to the department, but there is no data for the reporting period.

14
00:01:12.528 --> 00:01:16.076
Not Applicable means the metric does not apply to that department.

15
00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:20.591
Keeping these choices separate makes the reason for a submission without data clear.

16
00:01:21.291 --> 00:01:28.084
In step four, the department uploads supporting documents for the selected metric to the submission folder in Google Drive.

17
00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:35.595
The portal follows the shared upload workflow: editing access is available during upload, and changes to viewing after final submission.

18
00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.412
The documents support the data supplied for review.

19
00:01:39.112 --> 00:01:44.788
In step five, the user reviews the department details, selected metric, and submission information.

20
00:01:44.788 --> 00:01:48.802
They confirm the declaration checkboxes and complete final submission.

21
00:01:48.802 --> 00:01:53.791
This makes the departmental data and supporting documents available for quality review.

22
00:01:53.791 --> 00:02:03.080
Google Apps Script, Google Sheets, and Google Drive connect the collection process and help prepare clean, validated departmental information for NAAC submission.
